<stop> element:
The 'Stop' Element
The 'stop' element instructs a Job to stop with a BatchStatus of STOPPED. 
Stopping a Job can provide a temporary break in processing so that the operator can take some action before restarting the Job. 
The 'stop' element requires a 'restart' attribute that specifies the step where execution should pick up when the Job is restarted.



